  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/chennai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chennai</a>:Union minister <a href=\"/tag/jitendra+singh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Jitendra Singh</a> on Thursday called for greater use of emerging technologies to prevent disease and protect young people’s health.Addressing the <a href=\"/tag/42nd+convocation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">42nd convocation</a> of <a href=\"/tag/sri+ramachandra+institute+of+higher+education+and+research+%28sriher%29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sri Ramachandra Institute of Higher Education and Research (SRIHER)</a>, he said <a href=\"/tag/artificial+intelligence\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">artificial intelligence</a>, <a href=\"/tag/genomics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">genomics</a> and <a href=\"/tag/quantum+technologies\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">quantum technologies</a> were transforming medicine. He highlighted the growing burden of diabetes and coronary artery disease.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The Sequencing Atlas for National Genomics and Medicine (SANGAM) programme under the <a href=\"/tag/national+genomics+data+grid\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">National Genomics Data Grid</a> aimed to sequence the genomes of about one million genetically diverse Indians and link the information with clinical outcomes to advance personalised treatment.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>He presented 106 gold medals to meritorious students. University chancellor VR  Venkataachalam conferred degrees on 2,116 graduates across medical, engineering and management disciplines.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Presenting the annual report, medical college dean K Balaji Singh said SRIHER introduced 26 programmes and signed 25 collaboration agreements in 2025–26. The institution was also incubating more than 40 start-ups with funding from BIRAC-DBT.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                    \n\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 23, 2026 at 12:18 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 23, 2026 at 12:18 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/